=> H1 (refined): a fork made WHILE a no-copy page is wired copies the whole mapping eagerly (seconds, page-ins ≈ the file the first time); forks with the GPU idle are fast because the driver unwires between command buffers. A decode always has a command buffer in flight, so the 2 s swap-guard fork on M26 always pays it: 15 GB per tick.
